# Recorded from a second runtime; see docs/reference-runtime.md. The model is
# NOT committed -- see docs/fixture-provenance.md. No mandatory test reads
# this file.
#
# The vector below is what llama.cpp produced for this prompt, pooled and at
# unit length, recorded whole for the reason the other two are: a cosine
# taken over part of a vector says nothing about the rest.
#
# What this one is for is the slope ladder. This architecture learns no
# positions and rotates nothing; it is told where a token is by a fall-off
# in the attention scores, one slope a head. The ladder has two branches and
# the second is only reached by a head count that is not a power of two --
# twelve heads take eight rungs of the first and four of the second. A
# ladder written as the first branch alone is right for two thirds of the
# heads of this model and wrong for the rest, which is an embedding and not
# a refusal. That is why this variant and not the small one, whose eight
# heads would have agreed with the wrong ladder.
#
# It also decides three things a fixture cannot: that the fall-off is
# unsigned -- this model reads a whole text, so a position is as far from
# what follows it as from what came before -- that it is taken off after the
# scale by one over the root of the head width rather than before, and that
# eight is the number, which no published file of this architecture states
# and the other runtime carries in its own source.
#
# The weights are F16 for the reason the other two are: against a quantized
# file the two runtimes differ by the other one's activation quantization
# rather than by anything here.
#
# One note on reproducing it. llama.cpp's own llama-embedding aborts on this
# file -- it looks up an end-of-text identifier the file does not state --
# so the recording was taken with
#   --override-kv tokenizer.ggml.eos_token_id=int:102
# which is the identifier the file names as its separator and the one both
# runtimes wrap the text in anyway. The tokens either way are
# [101, 1037, 4937, 7719, 2006, 1996, 13523, 102].

runtime llama.cpp e85caa8
model jina-v2-base-en.f16.gguf
prompt a cat sits on the mat
pooling mean
tolerance 5.0E-04

